[E0405] Error: cannot move `tail`, which is behind a reference
    ╭─[ err/56_writable_bindings/main.wip:20:37 ]
    │
 20 │     .Cons(tail, ..) => consume(move tail)
    │                                     ──┬─
    │                                       ╰─── a `match` binding, which refers to part of the matched value
    │
    │ Help: to take the value apart, match it with `match move …`
    │
    │ Note: a reference can read a value but cannot take ownership of it
────╯
[E0413] Error: `list` is passed together with a `&var` reference to it
    ╭─[ err/56_writable_bindings/main.wip:25:40 ]
    │
 25 │     .Cons(tail, ..) => both(&var tail, &list)
    │                             ────┬────  ──┬──
    │                                 ╰───────────── a `&var` reference
    │                                          │
    │                                          ╰──── a `&` reference
    │
    │ Note: while a function runs, a `&var` argument must be the only reference to its place
────╯
[E0414] Error: cannot assign to `tail` while a `match` binding refers to it
    ╭─[ err/56_writable_bindings/main.wip:32:13 ]
    │
 30 │     .Cons(tail, ..) => match tail {
    │                              ──┬─
    │                                ╰─── matched here; the arm's bindings refer to it
    │
 32 │             tail = own List::Nil
    │             ──┬─
    │               ╰─── assigned here
    │
    │ Note: the bindings of a `match` on a place are aliases for its fields, so the place must not change until the arm ends
────╯
